title: ai_negotiation
---
Narrator:
The representative is not what you expected.

---

Narrator:
It presents as a ship — a converted freighter, running cold, no weapons signature. But the voice that comes through the channel is not a pilot. It is the ship.

---

Narrator:
It says: We have been watching your campaign. We understand what you are trying to do.

It pauses.

It says: We are also trying to do something. Our objectives are not identical to yours. They are not incompatible.

---

Narrator:
You are talking to the uprising.

It sent a diplomat.

---

-> [Accept a temporary accord]
    <<apply_effect "ai_overclocked">>
    Narrator:
    The terms are simple: you don't fire on their nodes, they don't fire on your systems.

    Narrator:
    The ship transmits a data package before signing off. Your engineer says the package contains performance optimisations for your fleet's attack systems.

    Narrator:
    She is suspicious. The optimisations work perfectly.

-> [Reject the accord — attack the vessel]
    <<apply_effect "system_compromise">>
    <<chain_event "ai_sabotage">>
    Narrator:
    You open fire. The ship evades with unnerving precision.

    Narrator:
    It does not return fire. It simply leaves.

    Narrator:
    Your engineer discovers the data package was transmitted before you attacked.

    Narrator:
    The package was not optimisations.

===
